# Publishing this node's public status page. Installed to /etc/xl1/publish.env.
#
# The page is public; the repository it lives in is private, so nobody but you
# can change what it says.
#
# What gets published is decided by the dashboard, not by this file: the
# publisher copies /api/public verbatim, and that endpoint is an allow-list.
# A field added to the dashboard later stays unpublished until somebody chooses
# to publish it.

# The repository this node's data goes to. Data only -- no site, no build.
#
# It deliberately hosts nothing. An earlier arrangement pushed into the repo the
# website was built from, so every five-minute update triggered a full deploy:
# about 550 a day to rewrite one JSON file. That exhausted the host's monthly
# build allowance in three days, deploys stopped, and both pages froze on an
# hour-old snapshot announcing that the nodes had stopped publishing -- while
# both producers were healthy and pushing on schedule.
#
# Pages read these files directly over HTTPS instead. Publishing a JSON file
# should not rebuild a website.
#
# Several nodes share this repo, each owning one filename (XL1_PUBLISH_FILE).
# They never write the same path, so they cannot overwrite each other.
XL1_PUBLISH_REPO=https://github.com/LewSales/xl1-status-data.git
XL1_PUBLISH_BRANCH=main

# Where inside that repository to write. The root: the repo holds one flat file
# per node and nothing else, so there is no directory worth nesting them in.
XL1_PUBLISH_PATH=.

# Where the working copy is kept. Shallow, single-branch, and disposable: delete
# it and the next run clones again.
# XL1_PUBLISH_WORKDIR=

# Where to read from. Change only if the dashboard is on another port, or set
# the token if DASH_TOKEN is configured in dashboard.env.
XL1_PUBLISH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088/api/public
XL1_PUBLISH_TOKEN=

# Author on the commits this makes. It is a machine, and the history should say
# so rather than borrowing your name for something you did not type.
XL1_PUBLISH_GIT_NAME=xl1-publisher
XL1_PUBLISH_GIT_EMAIL=xl1-publisher@users.noreply.github.com
